  "caveats": [
    "The initial build passed 63 tests; a fresh final build passed the added malformed-copy regression and strengthened witness-reuse regression. Production inputs and both runtime JARs are byte-identical across the two builds. The unique count deduplicates the repeated test; the exact test-only extension diff is retained.",
    "Real TCP histories reconstruct public bootstrap, two original phased publications, DATA image state and maintenance at stable sizes 3/4/5. Only two endpoints run during the copy; complete retained ancestry is obtained from one actual source. No copied ACK is counted as a new Owned observation.",
    "Adopted joint/final and removed-reader tests use actual local storage/transfer with conditional original membership force fixtures; they do not establish a full distributed member transition.",
    "This uses the frozen crash-fault/authentic-exclusive-replica assumption, not Byzantine/signature authentication. A private completed-transfer capability and exact manifest/packet bindings do not replace structural, endpoint, incarnation or majority checks.",
    "The complete receiving owners must stay live through use. The historical key set is bounded to the current packet plus the attached six-bridge set; it is not a durable reopening credential or deletion permission.",
    "Automatic cross-view adoption/elections, durable reopening, unavailable required ancestry, maximal combined lifetime, learner/joint completion, generalized publication and complete Phase 3 S/N qualification remain open."
  ],
